      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Boom colt LOUCASSO (7) was just too good in his comeback victory here a fortnight ago when he led from this barrier and kept going. That was his first outing for nearly nine months so should only be better for it. He is two from two when second-up and has to go on top. ALERT BAY (5) stuck on well for second to LOUCASSO last time, only 2.8m behind him. That added to a string of top-three results including a win from wider three back. He can be competitive again. ANDRETTI (3) was a class above when he led to score easily last week at Bathurst. This is harder but he draws to go forward again. THE QUEENS GAMBIT NZ (6) faces her toughest yet since switching from NZ but has been impressive in winning her two Australian starts so far, one at this circuit and distance when she overcome the outside barrier.",
